course: dictionary
lesson: 9666
title: Subtract: taking away to find what is left
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To subtract means to take one number away from another, to find what is left. It can also mean to take something away from a group or an amount. The sign for subtract is −, and the answer to a subtraction is the difference.
explain: «Then decide whether to add or subtract.» Before you calculate, ask: am I putting things together, or taking things away? If things go away, such as giving, losing, eating or breaking, you subtract. If you want to know how many more one thing is than another, you also subtract.
explain: Subtraction helps in everyday life. If a shop charges 3 pounds and you pay with 10 pounds, you subtract 3 from 10 to find your change. You can also subtract to find how much time is still to wait, or how many years lie between two dates.
fact: To subtract means to take one number away from another.
fact: Subtraction is the operation shown by the sign −, and the answer is called the difference.
fact: «Subtract 5 from 12» means 12 − 5 = 7, and it is the same as «take 5 away from 12».
fact: «Between two AD years, subtract» means you take the earlier year away from the later year to find how many years lie between them.
fact: Check your answer by adding back: 7 + 5 = 12, so 12 − 5 = 7 is right.
exercise: Sam has 12 sweets and eats 5. What do you do to find how many are left? | Divide 12 by 5 | *Subtract 5 from 12 | Add 12 and 5 | Multiply 12 by 5
exercise: «To compare, find each part and subtract the smaller from the bigger.» Half of 12 is 6 and a third of 12 is 4. How much more is the half? | 4 | 10 | *2 | 6
exercise: «Each capture takes one piece off the board, so subtract all the captures of both players from 32.» Suppose 9 pieces are captured in total. How many pieces are left? | 41 | 9 | 32 + 9 | *23
test: A class has 15 pencils and 6 are broken. Which calculation finds the pencils that still work? | 15 × 6 | *15 − 6 | 6 − 15 | 15 + 6
test: What is the difference between 20 and 13? | 13 | 33 | 27 | *7
exam: Which phrase means the same as subtract 5 from 12? | Multiply 5 by 12 | *Take 5 away from 12 | Take 12 away from 5 | Add 5 to 12
